/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 65 0 R
/T (Data integrity meansthatthe data stored in the database is accurate, consistent and follows the rules of the business. In a relational database, integrity is enforced by constraints. This assignment applies primary keys, foreign keys, UNIQUE, CHECK, DEFAULT and NOT NULL constraints to the eight tables of the Cab Booking Management System, explains why each one is needed, and then runs SQL statements to prove that invalid data is rejected and that valid data keeps the tables correctly connected.)
/E (Data integrity meansthatthe data stored in the database is accurate, consistent and follows the rules of the business. In a relational database, integrity is enforced by constraints. This assignment applies primary keys, foreign keys, UNIQUE, CHECK, DEFAULT and NOT NULL constraints to the eight tables of the Cab Booking Management System, explains why each one is needed, and then runs SQL statements to prove that invalid data is rejected and that valid data keeps the tables correctly connected.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
