/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 75 0 R
/T (Primary keys, foreignkeys, UNIQUE, CHECK, DEFAULT and NOT NULL constraints were applied to all eight tables and explained. The tests showed that duplicate keys, missing parent records, duplicate unique values, invalid statuses, out-of-range ratings and negative amounts are all rejected, that default values are filled in automatically, and that the one-to-one and one-to-many relationships are enforced by the database itself. The orphan-record queries returned zero violations, so the data remains consistent.)
