778 0 obj
<<
/Title (Data integrity meansthatthe data stored in the database is accurate, consistent and follows the rules of the business. In a relational database, integrity is enforced by constraints. This assignment applies primary keys, foreign keys, UNIQUE, CHECK, DEFAULT and NOT NULL constraints to the eight tables of the Cab Booking Management System, explains why each one is needed, and then runs SQL statements to prove that invalid data is rejected and that valid data keeps the tables correctly connected.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 703 0 R
/Next 779 0 R
>>
endobj
779 0 obj
<<
/Title (Most constraints were defined in the CREATE TABLE statements of Assignment 5. In this assignment they are reviewed and explained, a few extra constraints are added with ALTER TABLE, and every constraint is tested.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 703 0 R
/Prev 778 0 R
>>
endobj
